    {
      "id": "p0129-b006",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In English, the word \"eliminate\" usually means \"to get rid of something\" or even \"to kill\", but in some contexts - such as when discussing physiology or animal training- it can mean \"to expel waste matter from the body\". Toby made sure to mention this double meaning in his translation notes.",
        "raw": "In English, the word \"eliminate\" usually means \"to get rid of something\" or\neven \"to kill\", but in some contexts - such as when discussing physiology or\nanimal training- it can mean \"to expel waste matter from the body\". Toby\nmade sure to mention this double meaning in his translation notes.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.08891808,
          0.37854286,
          0.67526966,
          0.44632857
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.08507923,
          0.37782857,
          0.69270317,
          0.4474
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          17,
          18,
          19,
          20
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "英语的 eliminate 通常表示“清除某物”，甚至“杀死”；但在某些语境中，例如讨论生理或动物训练时，也可以表示“把废物排出体外”。Toby 特意在翻译说明中提到了这层双重含义。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
      "annotations": [],
